From 71ccb7967e475543534509aa3a03b57221e99892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <antbelkin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:08:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] player, vo_gpu_next: --video-join, two video tracks shown
 side by side

A 360 camera records each lens in a video track of its own. With
--video-join the first two video tracks of the same size and codec
are one picture: the second becomes a dependent track of the first,
as a Dolby Vision enhancement layer is, so the demuxer reads it along
and f_enhancement_pair decodes it with the same hardware decoding and
attaches each frame to the first track's of the same time. vo_gpu_next
maps both hardware surfaces and draws them side by side into planes of
the frame's own, on the GPU.

lavfi-complex's hstack did the same in memory: its tracks' decoders get
no hardware decoding device, so they decode to memory (VideoToolbox's
copy mode at best), and the joined frame is uploaded again.
---
